%description:

TcpVegas.alpha:invalid -- a threshold below 0 stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts 0 <= alpha <= beta.

The classes: linux (2, the default, the value of Linux tcp_vegas.c), zero (0: in congestion
avoidance, the window never grows), invalid (below 0, or above beta). The code: once
each round trip, TcpVegas::receivedAckForUnackedData() compares the extra segments, diff,
with the thresholds; TcpVegas::initializeAlgorithm() checks them.

Host under test: host1, with TcpVegas. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: TcpVegas.alpha
%# class: invalid
%# value: -1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.alpha
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpVegasAlphaInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.alpha = -1    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpVegas"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
the thresholds must be 0 <= alpha <= beta and 0 <= gamma, but alpha=-1, beta=4, gamma=1
